[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624807160","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102144#issuecomment-2624807160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102144","id":2624807160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cc2D4","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T15:26:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T15:26:24Z","body":"BTW, this is not related to this PR, but I remember that Quaternion's `is_normalized()` has a similar accuracy problem, so this might be a good opportunity to rethink the epsilon values.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624807160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626595867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102144#issuecomment-2626595867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102144","id":2626595867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cjqwb","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T08:17:55Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T15:01:13Z","body":"My first thoughts are, why is this epsilon needed at all? (Don't get me wrong, it could be required for detecting gimbal lock, but would be nice to confirm.)\r\n\r\nIf it is for `asin` (which errors outside -1 to 1), the `Math::asin()` is a safe version which won't error. I do however notice that for YXZ at line 540 it doesn't seem to be using the `Math` versions, that should be corrected, as we should prefer the Math versions especially for asin / acos because they are safe.\r\n\r\nI don't know if `atan2` has any strange out of range behaviour that the epsilons helped with, but from memory `atan2` is fairly robust (unless x and y are zero).\r\n\r\nHere's a gemini generated version for comparison:\r\n```\r\n// Function to extract Euler angles (ZYX order - Yaw, Pitch, Roll) from a rotation matrix (basis)\r\nEigen::Vector3d getEulerAnglesZYX(const Eigen::Matrix3d& rotationMatrix) {\r\n    double yaw, pitch, roll;\r\n\r\n    // Check for singularity (gimbal lock) -  pitch close to +/- 90 degrees\r\n    double sinPitch = -rotationMatrix(2, 0); //sin(pitch)\r\n    if (std::abs(sinPitch) >= 1.0) {\r\n        // Gimbal lock:  pitch = +/- 90 degrees.  Roll becomes undefined/arbitrary.\r\n        pitch = std::copysign(M_PI / 2.0, sinPitch); // pitch = +/- pi/2\r\n        yaw = std::atan2(-rotationMatrix(0, 2), rotationMatrix(1, 2)); // yaw becomes rotation around Z\r\n        roll = 0.0;  // Roll is undefined, set to 0 or any other value.\r\n        // Or handle differently, e.g., return a special \"gimbal lock\" indicator.\r\n    } else {\r\n        pitch = std::asin(sinPitch);\r\n        yaw = std::atan2(rotationMatrix(2, 1), rotationMatrix(2, 2));\r\n        roll = std::atan2(rotationMatrix(1, 0), rotationMatrix(0, 0));\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    return Eigen::Vector3d(yaw, pitch, roll); // Yaw, Pitch, Roll\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat said, this PR seems an improvement on the current behaviour and there's no reason we can't evaluate whether epsilons are required in a later PR. :+1: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626595867/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628557659","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102144#issuecomment-2628557659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102144","id":2628557659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6crJtb","user":{"login":"Cwazywierdo","id":42323315,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzIzMzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42323315?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo","html_url":"https://github.com/Cwazywierdo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cwazywierdo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T23:22:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T23:22:24Z","body":"While I was trying to determine the ideal epsilon value, I actually did consider getting rid of it entirely. When I looked at the PR that introduced it though (#39483), the author claimed that it solved a nondescript \"floating point issue.\" Without any other information on the actual issue, I figured it would be better to keep it and avoid a possible regression. I will change this if it's considered unnecessary.\r\n\r\nI will definitely go ahead and change those function calls to the Math versions though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628557659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628819198","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102144#issuecomment-2628819198","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102144","id":2628819198,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6csJj-","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T07:02:56Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T07:02:56Z","body":"Worth tagging @AndreaCatania and @RevoluPowered , I don't know if they are still contributing but they might remember why the epsilon was introduced.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628819198/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2631146633","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102144#issuecomment-2631146633","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102144","id":2631146633,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6c1ByJ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_